From 8886153046cf3cc727e657a8aaaf24f92c977bd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sandeep Sondagar <sandeepsondagar@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 23:48:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] qualcommbe: add JioRouter AX6000 (JIDU6J11 series)
 support

This adds OpenWrt support for the JioRouter AX6000 (JIDU6J11 series)
Wi-Fi 6 router based on Qualcomm IPQ9554. All five SKUs (JIDU6111,
JIDU6411, JIDU6611, JIDU6811, JIDU6911) share the same underlying
hardware baseline, differing only in physical antenna configuration.

Hardware specification:
- SoC: Qualcomm IPQ9554 (4x ARM Cortex-A73 @ 1.5 GHz)
- RAM: 512 MB DDR4
- Flash: 256 MB SPI NAND
- Ethernet: 5x 10/100/1000 Mbps (1 WAN + 4 LAN via QCA8075)
- WiFi 2.4 GHz: Integrated IPQ95XX AHB, 802.11b/g/n/ax, 4x4 MIMO (ath11k)
- WiFi 5 GHz: QCN9074 PCIe, 802.11a/n/ac/ax, 4x4 MIMO (ath11k)
- Expansion: 1x USB 3.0
- LEDs: 3x GPIO-controlled (Red, Green, Blue)
- Buttons: 1x Reset
- UART: 115200 8N1 (3.3V TX/RX/GND header on board)
- Power supply: 12V DC, 2.5A

MAC address layout:
- WAN / Label: ART partition, offset 0x00
- LAN: WAN + 1
- 2.4 GHz: WAN + 2
- 5 GHz: WAN + 3

SoC enablement backports:
- dt-bindings: clk: qcom: ipq9574: add WCSS Q6 clocks
- clk: qcom: gcc-ipq9574: add WCSS Q6 clocks
- remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_wcss: add IPQ9574 support

Dependencies: the integrated 2.4 GHz radio additionally requires the
companion "mac80211: enable IPQ9574 AHB support" and "mac80211: add
driver patches for IPQ9574" commits, which add the ath11k AHB driver
(qcom,ipq9574-wifi compatible) and the ath11k-firmware-ipq9574 board
firmware package. The qcom,ipq9574-wcss-pil remoteproc driver is
provided by the remoteproc backport listed above.

The base-files scripts extract the ath11k calibration data via
caldata_extract, set up the U-Boot mtdparts for the ubi partition, and
perform nand_do_upgrade for sysupgrade.

Note: each of the five SKUs is described by a separate device-tree file
because ath11k does not support nvmem-based calibration-variant lookups;
it only accepts the "qcom,ath11k-calibration-variant" value as a DT
string literal. Since each SKU needs its own board-specific BDF variant
string, a distinct compatible string and DTS file is required per SKU so
the correct calibration data gets selected.

Flashing instructions (TFTP + initramfs):
Note: "6111" in the image filenames is the SKU code; replace it with the
SKU code of your device (e.g. 6411, 6611, 6811 or 6911).
1. Connect a 3.3V USB-to-UART adapter to the serial header (115200 baud).
2. Set a static IP on your computer (e.g., 192.168.1.2/24).
3. Place the initramfs image into your TFTP server root directory:
   openwrt-qualcommbe-ipq95xx-jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j11-6111-initramfs-uImage.itb
4. Power on the router and interrupt autoboot in the serial console.
5. Boot the initramfs image from U-Boot:
   setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1
   setenv serverip 192.168.1.2
   tftpboot 0x44000000 openwrt-qualcommbe-ipq95xx-jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j11-6111-initramfs-uImage.itb
   bootm 0x44000000
6. Transfer the sysupgrade image to /tmp and flash it:
   sysupgrade /tmp/openwrt-qualcommbe-ipq95xx-jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j11-6111-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin

Signed-off-by: Sandeep Sondagar <sandeepsondagar@gmail.com>
